hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19230","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taifi narrated to us from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Aws al-Thaqafi from his grandfather Aws ibn Hudhayfah who said: I was among the delegation who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embracing Islam, from Thaqif of Banu Malik. He lodged us in a dome of his. He would visit us between his houses and the mosque. When he prayed the last Isha he went to us, and he kept talking to us and complaining of Quraysh and complaining of the people of Makkah. Then he would say: It is not equal; we were in Makkah humiliated or weakened, and when we went out to Madinah the fortunes of war were against us and for us. He stayed away from us one night and did not come to us until it was long after Isha. He said: We said: What kept you from us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A hizb of the Quran came upon me, and I wanted not to go out until I completed it. In the morning we asked the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: We said: How do you portion the Quran? They said: We portion it six surahs, five surahs, seven surahs, nine surahs, eleven surahs, thirteen surahs, and the hizb of the Mufassal from Qaf until the end."
